  {
   "id": "h218",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "07 — The Kit"
  },
  {
   "id": "h219",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "No barbell. <em>Goes anywhere.</em>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h220",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Minimal on purpose — this program goes anywhere. Bands, dumbbells, a box, and open space build a serious off-ice engine."
  },
  {
   "id": "h221",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Loop resistance bands"
  },
  {
   "id": "h222",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Light–moderate dumbbells"
  },
  {
   "id": "h223",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Pull-up bar (optional)"
  },
  {
   "id": "h224",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "A low box or bench"
  },
  {
   "id": "h225",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Space to move"
  },
  {
   "id": "h226",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "An open stretch for sprints"
  },
  {
   "id": "h227",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Done at home, in a garage, or at a field. This is your speed, power &amp; conditioning work — pair it with your barbell strength work when you can."
  },
  {
   "id": "h228",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "08 — How It Trains"
  },
  {
   "id": "h229",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Built to <em>peak.</em>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h230",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<b>Full intent, every rep.</b> Speed and power only improve when you're fresh and firing. We program quality over grinding — short, fast, maximal efforts with real rest between them."
  },
  {
   "id": "h231",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<b>Peak, then unload.</b> Intensity climbs for three weeks, then deliberately backs off. Weeks 4 and 8 deload so you arrive at every checkpoint sharp and fast — not buried under fatigue."
  },
  {
   "id": "h232",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "09 — Questions"
  },
  {
   "id": "h233",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Good to <em>know.</em>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h234",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>Will this replace my gym strength work?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h235",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "No — and it's not meant to. This is the off-ice speed, power, and conditioning engine, built with bands, bodyweight, and dumbbells. It won't build a maximal back-squat or deadlift — that needs a barbell. Pair it with your gym strength work when you can; together they're a complete program."
  },
  {
   "id": "h236",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>Do I need a gym?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h237",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "No gym required. Bands, dumbbells, a box, and open space — it goes anywhere: home, garage, or a field. The sprint tests just need a longer open stretch."
  },
  {
   "id": "h238",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>How is the program delivered?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h239",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "It's a clean, interactive web program you open on any phone, tablet, or laptop — with a demo video built into every exercise. No PDF to lose, no app to install. Buy once and it's yours forever."
  },
  {
   "id": "h240",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>How much time does each session take?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h241",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "About 55–70 minutes, four times a week. Every session follows the same five-part shape and includes the built-in RAMP warm-up. Run them in order; the plan does the thinking for you."
  },
  {
   "id": "h242",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>Will it actually make me faster?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h243",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Trained with intent, yes — measurably faster, more explosive, more powerful side-to-side, and better conditioned, and the five skill-check tests prove it in real numbers. The one thing it won't do is build a maximal squat — that's barbell work."
  },
  {
   "id": "h244",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>Is it too late to start before the season?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h245",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "No — and waiting for a &quot;perfect&quot; start date is the real mistake. If a full 8 weeks fits before your season, you arrive at day one at your peak. If the season starts sooner, the first weeks of speed and power work still show up on the ice within a month — and the program runs fine alongside early-season practices (drop to two or three sessions in heavy game weeks). Every week you wait is a week of the season played without it."
  },
  {
   "id": "h246",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>What if it's not the right fit?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h247",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "You're covered by a 30-day money-back guarantee. Try it, run the first sessions, and if it isn't right for you, just email us and we'll refund you — no hassle."
  },
  {
